<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n24319" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δηλᾰδή</span></b>  (cf. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δῆλος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					11.4
				</span></i>
			), Adv.
			<i>clearly, manifestly,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Epich.
				149
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>OT</u>
				1501
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>IA</u>
				1366
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Timocl.
				3
			</span></i>
			<i><span class="en">
				D.
			</span></i>, etc.: ironically, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">προφάσιος τῆσδε
				δηλαδή</span> on this pretext <i>forsooth,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				4.135
			</span></i>: freq. in answers, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐ πόλλ᾽ ἔνεστι δεινὰ τῷ γήρᾳ
					κακά;—δηλαδή</span>”
				<i>yes plainly, of course,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>V.</u>
					441
				</span></i>
			: but better written divisim in such phrases as 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἢ δῆλα δὴ ὅτι . .;</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Prt.</u>
					309a
				</span></i>
			, etc.; cf. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δῆλα δὴ καὶ ταῦτα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Cri.</u>
					48b
				</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
